Description: Drag tiled windows like i3: tiling_drag modes, insert, swap_modifier
 Regolith runs i3 and sway from one configuration. i3's tiling_drag takes
 a choice of drag styles, and its default config ships "tiling_drag
 modifier titlebar"; sway rejected that line (a configuration error at
 every login) and read "tiling_drag modifier" or "tiling_drag titlebar"
 as off. sway now accepts off, modifier, titlebar and both styles in
 either order; the boolean words keep working, toggle switches between
 off and both styles, and any other argument is an error.
 .
 A tiled window dropped on the middle of another one now goes right
 after it in its parent (a new tab or stack entry in tabbed and stacked
 containers), as in i3. The two swap only if the swap modifier was held
 when the drag began: "tiling_drag swap_modifier <modifier>" takes the
 names floating_modifier takes, + combinations as i3 writes them, or
 none; Shift is the default. A swap reports a window move event for each
 window.
 .
 A modifier drag no longer focuses the dragged window, as in i3, and a
 swap keeps the focus where it was, also when the two windows are on
 different outputs. A title bar drag focuses the window like a click.
 With only title bar drags enabled, holding the floating modifier does
 not skip tiling_drag_threshold.
 .
 Applied on top of 12-i3-tree-moves: the swap keeps the focused node in
 its focus path instead of moving the focus to the window that takes its
 place.
